    "phrases": [
      {
        "scene": "S01",
        "text": "What if a city suddenly began dancing—and could not stop?",
        "start": 0.0,
        "end": 4.16
      },
      {
        "scene": "S01",
        "text": "In Strasbourg, in the summer of 1518, one exhausted woman began to move in the street.",
        "start": 4.86,
        "end": 11.68
      },
      {
        "scene": "S01",
        "text": "Then another joined her.",
        "start": 12.3,
        "end": 13.8
      },
      {
        "scene": "S01",
        "text": "Soon, the city was watching a frightening outbreak no one understood.",
        "start": 14.2,
        "end": 18.46
      },
      {
        "scene": "S02",
        "text": "The dancers multiplied.",
        "start": 19.34,
        "end": 20.96
      },
      {
        "scene": "S02",
        "text": "Some moved for hours, some for days, while horrified neighbors watched their strength disappear.",
        "start": 21.82,
        "end": 27.68
      },
      {
        "scene": "S02",
        "text": "The exact numbers remain uncertain—but the terror they left behind became notorious.",
        "start": 27.68,
        "end": 34.32
      },
      {
        "scene": "S03",
        "text": "The authorities searched for a cure and made a desperate decision: give the dancers room, and bring in musicians.",
        "start": 35.48,
        "end": 43.0
      },
      {
        "scene": "S03",
        "text": "They believed movement might burn the sickness out.",
        "start": 43.74,
        "end": 46.84
      },
      {
        "scene": "S03",
        "text": "Instead, the remedy risked feeding the spectacle.",
        "start": 47.48,
        "end": 51.02
      },
      {
        "scene": "S04",
        "text": "But the music could not hide the cost.",
        "start": 52.26,
        "end": 54.52
      },
      {
        "scene": "S04",
        "text": "Chroniclers described bodies driven past exhaustion and people collapsing in the streets.",
        "start": 54.52,
        "end": 61.2
      },
      {
        "scene": "S04",
        "text": "Later retellings speak of mass deaths, though the surviving evidence cannot firmly prove those numbers.",
        "start": 61.98,
        "end": 68.607
      },
      {
        "scene": "S05",
        "text": "Centuries later, the mystery still resists a single answer.",
        "start": 69.8,
        "end": 73.96
      },
      {
        "scene": "S05",
        "text": "Historians have considered famine and stress, belief, disease, and social contagion—but no surviving evidence proves one cause beyond doubt.",
        "start": 74.82,
        "end": 85.861
      },
      {
        "scene": "S06",
        "text": "What remains is more disturbing than a ghost story: a real city confronting behavior it could not control, while its leaders acted without understanding what they were seeing.",
        "start": 87.36,
        "end": 98.86
      },
      {
        "scene": "S06",
        "text": "The strangest part was not that people danced.",
        "start": 99.54,
        "end": 102.12
      },
      {
        "scene": "S06",
        "text": "It was that everyone around them watched—and joined in.",
        "start": 102.7,
        "end": 105.917
      }
    ],
